    "updated_at": "2021-08-08T02:05:33Z",
    "body": "I'm not following - the spec doesn't seem to do that?  If the last value parses as a number, we use the IPv4 parser, and if it fails, we reject the hostname.  The number parser parses both 4294967295 and 4294967296.  There's also the all ASCII digits fallback, but that's not needed here, anyways, since the IPv4 number parser doesn't have a limit of 2^32-1.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
